      "challenges": [
        "3,093 alerts; 3,093 verified (100.0%), 498 validated suspects, 498 investigated (100.0%), and 268 transferred. Six provinces have numeric alert rows (Haut-Uele, Bas-Uele, Ituri, Nord-Kivu, Sud-Ubangi and Tshopo); Sud-Kivu is unavailable, not zero.",
        "Nord-Kivu prints 417 hospitalised patients (139 confirmed, 278 suspected), 271 of them in normed structures, and 74.2% occupancy as 271/365, its first printed bed count since SR135. On the comparable all-patient basis 417/365 is 114.2%, which is promoted; the printed normed-structure rate is preserved. 146 patients (35.0%) are outside normed structures.",
        "Contact follow-up 23,741/29,535 (80.4%). The six province rows sum exactly to the national 23,741/29,535. Sud-Kivu is unavailable, not zero. The national rate moved from 79.7% the day before, and no province followed all of its contacts.",
        "PoE/PoC Table 4 reports two alerts. At the Tchomia PoC (Ituri), the body of a woman coming from Uganda for burial in Tchomia was intercepted and swabbed, result pending. At the PK5 PoC (Nord-Kivu), a 33-year-old Ugandan driver travelling from Beni towards Uganda with vomiting, diarrhoea, chills and asthenia was validated as a suspect but not evacuated for lack of an ambulance (0/1 transferred). Tshopo reporting completeness fell to 8/18 (44.4%) because ten private ports in Makiso-Kisangani do not operate on Sundays.",
        "Ituri ring opening is 20/40 (50.0%) and 59 of 96 safe and dignified burial alerts were completed (61.5%), with 29 failures. In Nord-Kivu, ring opening is 45/63 (71.4%), household decontamination 18/63 (28.6%) and the mean infection-prevention score of 35 assessed facilities 37.8%.",
        "Bas-Uele has 19 of 41 PoC notification sites functional (46.3%) and no reinforced PoE (0/11). In Haut-Uele, 159 travellers refused screening and 175 handwashing, amid rumours that the water and thermometers carry the virus."
      ],
      "priorities": [
        "Rapidly increase reception capacity in treatment centres in Nord-Kivu.",
        "Strengthen cross-border surveillance with South Sudan.",
        "Strengthen BDBV preparedness and response in the river-corridor provinces and surrounding areas."
      ],
